{"version":"1","id":"sass","handle":"sass","name":"Sass","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/95fc679f41e14ee08169554ea8e44d36","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.3172,"y":1.5695,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":12,"newest_post_at":"2025-10-24T23:19:17.023Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-10-30T13:14:12.007Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":4.0,"summary_length_avg":341.833333,"title_length_avg":37.666667,"title_length_var":77.555556,"tag_entropy":1.723714,"tag_diversity":0.583333,"top_tag_share":0.166667,"avg_upvotes":3.75,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.416667,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.130435,"zero_engagement_share":0.25,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.077035,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.090909},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.0735,8.5588],"cadence_depth":[-9.5882,-4.6912],"hype_variety":[-9.4559,-9.5588],"title_style":[-9.3088,-2.8235]},"top_tags":[["css",7],["webdev",5],["frontend",3],["javascript",2],["nodejs",2],["dart",1],["browsers",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Sass: `@import` is Deprecated","Sass: Node Sass is end-of-life","Sass: Request for Comments: Indented Syntax Improvements"],"outlier":["Sass: Sass in the Browser"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"KUIMHB1C2","title":"Sass: LibSass Has Reached End-Of-Life","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/libsass-is-end-of-life/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-libsass-has-reached-end-of-life-kuimhb1c2","summary":"LibSass, the C++ implementation of Sass, has officially reached end-of-life after being deprecated in October 2020. The project has seen no commits since December 2023 and will receive no future updates. Dart Sass now covers all LibSass use cases and supports modern CSS features like color spaces. Developers still using LibSass should migrate to Dart Sass, checking for deprecation warnings and visual differences. The Sass migrator tool can help automate some migration tasks.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-24T23:19:17.023Z"},{"id":"tNrYSY5I0","title":"Sass: Request for Comments: Indented Syntax Improvements","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/rfc-indented-syntax/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-request-for-comments-indented-syntax-improvements-tnrysy5i0","summary":"Sass is proposing new improvements to the indented syntax, addressing the long-standing issue of line breaks that don't end statements. The proposal includes multiline statements, SCSS format opt-in for individual blocks, and optional usage of semicolons. These changes are opt-in and won't require modifications to existing stylesheets.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-03T23:48:00.803Z"},{"id":"L80LB6bf2","title":"Sass: `@import` is Deprecated","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/import-is-deprecated/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-import-is-deprecated-l80lb6bf2","summary":"The `@import` rule in Sass is officially deprecated as of Dart Sass 1.80.0, to be fully removed by Dart Sass 3.0.0. Developers are encouraged to migrate to the module system using `@use` and `@forward`, which offer better maintainability and avoid CSS duplication. Tools and commands are provided to silence deprecation warnings or treat `@import` as an error to facilitate the transition.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-10-17T00:15:12.636Z"},{"id":"BmQU8aAH3","title":"Sass: Sass color spaces & wide gamut colors","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/wide-gamut-colors-in-sass/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-sass-color-spaces-wide-gamut-colors-bmqu8aah3","summary":"Sass introduces support for various color spaces and wide gamut colors, enhancing the precision and quality of colors in web design. These features allow developers to utilize a broader range of colors, improving the visual experience on modern displays that support wider color gamuts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e842849660e33b629146fbebb1cd0b2a?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-11T21:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"wBPzmPBx4","title":"Sass: Node Sass is end-of-life","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/node-sass-is-end-of-life/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-node-sass-is-end-of-life-wbpzmpbx4","summary":"Node Sass, a Node.js wrapper for LibSass, is now end-of-life due to lack of updates and maintainers. Users are encouraged to migrate to Dart Sass, the primary implementation. The npm package has been deprecated and the GitHub repository archived to avoid confusion. LibSass, while still deprecated, continues to receive occasional fixes but lacks official support for Node.js.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2024-07-24T22:05:59.895Z"},{"id":"ytb9adWmY","title":"Sass: Announcing `pkg:` Importers","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/announcing-pkg-importers/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-announcing-pkg-importers-ytb9adwmy","summary":"Announcement of the new `pkg:` importers feature in Dart Sass 1.71.0. The feature eliminates the need to manually add `node_modules` to loadPaths and improves portability. It allows anyone to implement custom importers to load packages from different package managers, maintaining consistent URLs. The post also explains how `pkg:` URLs work and provides guidance on publishing npm packages that work with the Node.js pkg: importer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a611ea74933e23fe5cc03236fda074d5?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-16T01:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"5SXBSBk3J","title":"Sass: Request for Comments: Package Importer","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/rfc-package-importer/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-request-for-comments-package-importer-5sxbsbk3j","summary":"Sass users often need to use styles from a dependency to customize an existing theme or access styling utilities. Historically, Sass has not specified a standard method for using packages from dependencies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a611ea74933e23fe5cc03236fda074d5?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-26T22:56:30.074Z"},{"id":"YQ3xfXsDR","title":"Sass: Sass in the Browser","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/sass-in-the-browser/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-sass-in-the-browser-yq3xfxsdr","summary":"With the release of Dart Sass 1.63, we\u2019re officially adding support to the npm package for running directly in the browser. No longer do creators of playgrounds or web IDEs need to make server calls to compile their Sass. You can just load it up and use it right on your very page.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a611ea74933e23fe5cc03236fda074d5?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-07T22:30:00.000Z"},{"id":"rR3qvm3UD","title":"Sass: Request for Comments: New Embedded Protocol","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/rfc-embedded-protocol-2","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-request-for-comments-new-embedded-protocol-rr3qvm3ud","summary":"The Embedded Sass Protocol will no longer be released as a separate executable. It will now be bundled into the main Dart Sass executable, accessible by running. Every packet in the embedded protocol now includes a compilation ID as part of the packet structure, rather than declaring it in the protocol buffer definitions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"GwieuSW0a","title":"Sass: Sass and Native Nesting","url":"https://sass-lang.com/blog/sass-and-native-nesting","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sass-sass-and-native-nesting-gwieusw0a","summary":"Chrome 112 is the first stable browser to add support for the new [native CSS nesting feature. This feature adds the ability to nest style rules in plain CSS, and even uses Sass\u2019s convention of to refer to the parent selector. Native CSS nesting has no way to add a suffix to a selector like Sass.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-29T22:51:34.206Z"}],"similar_handles":["taro","systemdesigncodex","planetxamarin","growthdesign","nette"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","hamelhusain"],"similar":[{"id":"taro","handle":"taro","name":"Taro","is_squad":false,"x":-6.3174,"y":1.6846,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":39,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/260164ce5b864765b44b2ed53e3e7b4c","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.429045,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.038462,"avg_read_time":5.641026,"tag_diversity":0.897436},"top_tags_preview":[["career",10],["big-tech",8],["internship",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.4412,7.0588],"cadence_depth":[-5.5882,-0.6176],"hype_variety":[7.5294,0.4706],"title_style":[-5.7647,6.1471]}},{"id":"systemdesigncodex","handle":"systemdesigncodex","name":"System Design Codex","is_squad":false,"x":-6.437,"y":1.6544,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":118,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/0df89304c19443509ec91a6ccb707853","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.0510